p: .
t. 
|  In theory, appellate courts exist to correct errors made at the trial level,
|  in family courts as in other courts. However, the cases we have reviewed
.  show that appellate review is rarely of much help to protective parents


--- Sentence/switch
id: 37
r#  21172  315  73


--- Sentence//end
id: 37
r#  21415  319  17
p: .
t. 
|  Appeals from family court rulings, particularly when an abuse or neglect
|  finding is at issue, rarely result in reversal of the lower court’s rulings; in
|  fact, the decisions usually uphold the family courts without even giving
.  detailed reasons

--- Sentence/end 
id: 37
